{
  "course": "international-macroeconomics",
  "title": "International Macroeconomics",
  "description": "Original constructed exercises for upper undergraduate and MA international macroeconomics. Prerequisites: intermediate microeconomics and macroeconomics, single-variable calculus and constrained optimization, present-value accounting, probability and conditional expectations, and introductory econometrics. Students should distinguish stocks from flows and gross from net rates. The course emphasizes external adjustment, exchange-rate conventions, financing frictions and identification; it does not reproduce trade-pattern models or the closed-economy graduate macro core. All numerical scenarios are hypothetical; official university materials guide topic coverage rather than supplying copied questions or empirical claims.",
